    {
      "segment_id": "S00001",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 174,
      "text": "MEXICO\nAnnex VI. Fiscal Policies to Tackle the Effects of Inflation in\nMexico\nThis annex considers the effects of rising fuel and food on households in Mexico and government\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00002",
      "start_char": 174,
      "end_char": 371,
      "text": "policies to cushion their impact. Poverty – officially measured using the cost of a basic basket of\nnecessities as a poverty line – has showed modest improvements since its peak in 2020 but rising\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00003",
      "start_char": 371,
      "end_char": 568,
      "text": "prices are exerting pressure on the poor. The government’s fuel pricing mechanism has helped to\nrestrain the effect of fuel price volatility on headline inflation in 2022 but only by subsuming the\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00004",
      "start_char": 568,
      "end_char": 771,
      "text": "sizable oil revenue gains that Mexico has accrued as an oil exporter. Measures to tackle rising food\nprices have leveraged and scaled up, albeit to a limited extent, pre-existing social and agricultural\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 771,
      "end_char": 939,
      "text": "support programs. In addition, both public and private sectors have taken steps to limit the pass-\nthrough of high prices to consumers, though the impact is not clear.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 939,
      "end_char": 1123,
      "text": "1. Rising prices and other essential items have put further strains on the poor on the\nheels of an increase in poverty since the pandemic. By the end of 2020, rural poverty had posted\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1123,
      "end_char": 1311,
      "text": "a modest improvement, with around 56.8 percent of the rural population in poverty or extreme\npoverty compared to 57.7 percent in 2018. However, the same period also saw a deterioration of\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1311,
      "end_char": 1507,
      "text": "conditions in urban areas, with around 40.1 percent of urban households estimated to be in some\nform of poverty—up from 36.8 percent in 2018—as illness and public health restrictions affected the\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1507,
      "end_char": 1690,
      "text": "economy (CONEVAL, 2022). Despite signs of a modest recovery, rising inflation strained real\nincomes in 2021, with price pressures from processed foods, including imported ones, a key\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
      "start_char": 1690,
      "end_char": 1885,
      "text": "contributor (IMF, 2021). Since then, rising food price inflation has continued to exert pressure on the\npoor, with the price of the minimum food consumption basket—the minimum food basket that a\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00011",
      "start_char": 1885,
      "end_char": 2120,
      "text": "household should be able to consume to ensure adequate nutrition and the extreme poverty line\nused in Mexico—rising by close to 2 percent for both rural and urban households between March\nand June of this year.\n125\n120\n115\n110\n105\n100\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00012",
      "start_char": 2120,
      "end_char": 2340,
      "text": "Dec-19 Apr-20 Aug-20 Dec-20 Apr-21 Aug-21 Dec-21 Apr-22\nSources: U.S. Department of Energy, PEMEX, CONEVAL; IMF staff calculations\n1/ The U.S. Gulf Coast price for conventional gasoline is an international market price.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00013",
      "start_char": 2340,
      "end_char": 2502,
      "text": "2/ The basic food basket, Canasta Alimentaria, is a basket of foodstuffs that are judged to provide minimum sufficient nutrition. The cost of this basket is used\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00014",
      "start_char": 2502,
      "end_char": 2651,
      "text": "to determine the extreme poverty lines in Mexico, with households whose income is insufficient to afford the basket judged to be in extreme poverty.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00015",
      "start_char": 2651,
      "end_char": 2868,
      "text": "3/ Per Capita Labor Income is defined as income from work, including both formal and informal work.\n4/ Data on per capita labor income is missing for 2020Q2 due the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on data collection.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00016",
      "start_char": 2868,
      "end_char": 3045,
      "text": "2. The authorities have launched a wide-ranging package of measures to tackle the\nimpact of rising inflation on households in 2022, with fuel subsidies front-and-center. As the\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00017",
      "start_char": 3045,
      "end_char": 3283,
      "text": "effects of rising inflation began to hit households in early 2022, the Mexican government launched a\npackage of measures to mitigate the impact under the name Paquete Contra La Inflación y La\nINTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND 69\n001\n= 9102\nceD\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00018",
      "start_char": 3283,
      "end_char": 3460,
      "text": ",xednI\nEvolution of Basic Food Basket Costs 2/\n100\n90\n80\n70\n60\n50\n40\nUrban 30\nRural\n20\natipaC\nreP emocnI\nfo tnecreP\nGasoline Prices 1/ Cost of Basic Food Basket as Share of Per\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00019",
      "start_char": 3460,
      "end_char": 3639,
      "text": "(Pesos per liter, monthly average) Capita Labor Income 3/ 4/ 30\nU.S. Gulf coast\n25 Mexico retail price (incl. VAT)\n20\n15\n10\nUrban\nRural 5\n0\n2001 2004 2007 2010 2013 2016 2019 2022"
