      "text": "from an increase in oil revenues due to rising oil prices at the same time that it has subsidized the\nhigher cost of fuel for domestic consumers, who largely consume refined oil product imports. While\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1654,
      "end_char": 1852,
      "text": "domestic fuel subsidies are expected to cost MEX$395.4 billion, the windfall gain in oil revenues\nrelative to the 2022 budget approved in 2021 is estimated at MEX$397.8 billion, suggesting that oil\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
